# Template for the CC / HK GitHub witness credential.
#
# DO NOT put a real credential in this file, or in any file in this repository.
# This is a shape reference only: the real value is installed by
# `install-github-witness-credential.sh` on the target host, read from stdin.
#
# What the credential must be:
#   type            fine-grained personal access token (read-only)
#   repository      yuguangzhi3836-glitch/GO     <- ONLY this repository
#   permissions     Actions     Read
#                   Contents    Read
#                   Metadata    Read   (mandatory for fine-grained PATs)
#
# What it must NOT have:
#   any write permission, administration, secrets, workflows, members,
#   deployments, packages, issues, pull requests.
#
# Where it goes (mode 0600):
#   cc  /etc/go-command-center/keys/github-witness-reader.token   owner root:root
#   hk  /etc/go-hk-agent/keys/github-witness-reader.token         owner go-hk-agent:go-hk-agent
#
# Purpose: GO C13/C14 Lite acceptance witness: GitHub Actions readback only.
#
# Note on the file this credential must NOT be confused with:
#   /etc/go-command-center/keys/github-requests-reader.token
# is an existing fine-grained PAT that authenticates as chenzhenxi1-sudo but has
# `/repos/yuguangzhi3836-glitch/GO` outside its repository selection, so every
# Actions read answers 404. It is left untouched; it belongs to another surface.
# The angle brackets are deliberate: a real value cannot contain them, so the secret
# scanner stays strict and still fires on an actual token pasted in here by mistake.
github_pat_<REPLACE_WITH_THE_REAL_VALUE>
